  "terrainName": "test-town",
  "description": "What: CE-4648 (R-1066) - an Afghan village: 36 civilians of the six Afghan types (types 1111-1116: man, woman, boy, girl, elderly man, elderly woman) stand near and far round a square, and three Afghan fighters (types 2016 rifle, 2017 RPG + rifle, 2018 machine gunner) hold a post to the north. Everyone is on the Idle behaviour. Judge: (1) every villager exists as its type and stays alive; (2) the fighters hold their post (they do not wander); (3) nobody is hurt. Look: the people are dressed from their Afghan wardrobes - perahan tunban, waistcoat, pakol, lungee turban, patu, chadari; the fighters with a chest rig and a turban or pakol. Fail: a person is missing, dead, or a fighter leaves his post."
 },
